    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1763">

                <pb facs="1435" n="1319" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1319"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 810.00/145.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Minister to
                        Guatemala</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-01-11T12:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 11, 1912—12 noon</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>When you have received the telegram of January 10, 2 p.m., from the American
                    Minister to Salvador, you will immediately take up this matter with the
                    President of Guatemala, vigorously impressing upon him the absolute necessity of
                    putting a stop to this hostile movement against Salvador, in utter disregard of
                    the Washington conventions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
